Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: let the root ports go to D3hot in system suspend without native pciehp

NOT YET FOR RELEASE: the default-on form of kit revision 11's debug switch
(pcie-qcom-debug-root-port-d3.patch, sleep-test.sh's root-port-d3).  It
has run as that switch three times on the SM-X710 (2026-11-23, revision
11's runs 3 to 5: once at pm_test=platform, twice in a real
suspend-to-idle), and never at boot, in the boot's panel cycle, on the
SM-X910 (whose Wi-Fi is another chip, on ath12k) or in a real deep sleep;
it needs more hardware passes before it ships.
scripts/build-mainline-kernel.sh applies this only with
APPLY_SM8550_ROOT_PORT_D3=1, which needs APPLY_SM8550_PCIE0_GDSC_OFF=1 and
APPLY_SM8550_PCIE0_GDSC_GUARD=1 (a host that powers down under
pcie_0_gdsc kept in retention is the sleep that never came back, 8 times of
8 on kit revisions 7 to 10), and refuses any other build in a tree that
carries it.  No board check.

Why.  A qcom PCIe host powers itself down in a system suspend only when
every function on its bus is in D3hot, its root port included
(pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(), from dw_pcie_suspend_noirq()), and the
PCI core puts the root port in D3hot only with bridge_d3
(pci_power_manageable(), from pci_pm_suspend_noirq()).  The qcom root
ports are hot-plug capable again since 33a76fc3c3e6 (v7.1), and
pci_bridge_d3_possible() refuses D3 to a hot-plug port that pciehp does
not handle natively before anything else: without CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE
(this port's configuration, and arm64's defconfig) pciehp_is_native() is
false, so with the Wi-Fi bound the root port stays in D0 and the host keeps
its link, clocks, PHY and votes through every suspend.  On the SM-X710
such a sleep kept pcie_0_gdsc and CX on (revision 11's run 2, a deep
sleep with the PCI devices kept: pcie_0_gdsc +0 and cx +0 in genpd's
power-offs, ddr +0), where one with the PCI devices removed collapsed both
(run 1, suspend-to-idle: pcie_0_gdsc +1, cx +1, ddr +1275); with the debug
switch the host powered down with the Wi-Fi bound and the sleep went as
the removed port's (runs 4 and 5, suspend-to-idle: pcie_0_gdsc +1, cx +1,
ddr +1261 and +1, the Wi-Fi back with one firmware load).

What upstream intends.  Root ports go to D3 on non-x86 (a5fb3ff63287 for
ports that are not hot-plug capable), and since d4c79b63d82d (v7.3,
Manivannan Sadhasivam, the qcom PCIe maintainer) hot-plug capable ones as
well, but only with native pciehp: upstream's route is
CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE=y, with 65ccb2203ef8 (v7.3) clearing Attention
Button Present for pciehp.  (On v7.2-rc3 a hot-plug port with native
pciehp is refused too, for being one, unless pcie_port_pm=force:
pci_bridge_d3_possible() before d4c79b63d82d.)  This port's kits cannot
change the kernel configuration (make-kit.sh requires the hang-log kit's),
and pciehp would bind to the port and act on its link-down and link-up
events at every suspend, which has not run here.  So this gives the root
port of a qcom host bridge_d3 where it is a hot-plug port without native
pciehp, the D3 that the PCI core of v7.3 gives the same port with native
pciehp, which is what the debug switch did by hand: the community SM8550
kernels get the same with CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE=y and pcie_port_pm=force
(ROCKNIX).

What changes, at every system suspend from the boot on, the boot's panel
cycle (pm_test=platform, about 22 s in) included: the root port goes to
D3hot after the Wi-Fi does; the host sends PME_Turn_Off, waits for L2/L3
Ready at most 10 ms (the WCN6855, reset by ath11k's suspend, never acks:
"Timeout waiting for L2 entry! LTSSM: 0x12", non-fatal since eed390775470),
powers the Wi-Fi off through pwrctrl and itself down; the guard marks it
out-of-band and genpd collapses pcie_0_gdsc; the resume sets the host up,
trains the link (0.27 s in revision 11's runs; the link wait gives up after
about 3.7 s on the SM-X710, pcie-dwc-link-wait-longer-gts9wifi.patch, and
0.9 s on the SM-X910) and restores the root port's and the Wi-Fi's
configuration, and the Wi-Fi driver loads its firmware as it does after
every suspend already (ath11k on the SM-X710).
Risks: a link that does not train at the resume loses the Wi-Fi until the
next boot, at every boot if it is the panel cycle's; a bus error at the
host's first access after the collapse would restart the tablet.  The
PCI core does not manage this port's bridge_d3 (pci_bridge_d3_update()
returns for a port pci_bridge_d3_possible() refuses), so a function's
D3cold veto (no_d3cold, d3cold_allowed 0 in sysfs) is not consulted for
it, and pcie_port_pm=off does not reach it; the in-tree ath11k and ath12k
set no such veto, and no PCI quirk does.
verify.sh's guard check expects the panel cycle to keep the link and would
note this boot's "the host powered down" line instead: to be adapted when
this ships.  pcie_qcom.root_port_d3=0 on the command line turns it off.
On a build with the debug switches too (APPLY_DEEP_SLEEP_DEBUG_SWITCHES=1)
the root port's debug switch still reads N at boot although the ports go
to D3hot from the boot on: its N takes it away until the restart, its Y
gives it back, and sleep-test.sh's root-port-d3 adds nothing there.

---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/units.h>
+#include <linux/pci_hotplug.h>
 
 #include "../../pci.h"
 #include "../pci-host-common.h"
@@ -2407,6 +2408,71 @@ DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QC
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x1000, qcom_fixup_class);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x1001, qcom_fixup_class);
 
+/*
+ * Root ports to D3hot in system suspend, so that a host powers itself down
+ * with its endpoint bound (pcie-qcom-root-port-d3-in-system-suspend.patch,
+ * APPLY_SM8550_ROOT_PORT_D3=1; test builds until it has run on hardware).
+ *
+ * A host powers itself down in a system suspend only when every function
+ * on its bus is in D3hot, its root port included
+ * (pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(), from dw_pcie_suspend_noirq()), and the
+ * PCI core puts a root port in D3hot only with bridge_d3
+ * (pci_power_manageable(), from pci_pm_suspend_noirq()).  The qcom root
+ * ports are hot-plug capable (33a76fc3c3e6, v7.1), and
+ * pci_bridge_d3_possible() refuses D3 to a hot-plug port that pciehp does
+ * not handle natively: a kernel without CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE (which this
+ * port's configuration leaves out) never gives them bridge_d3, so with the
+ * Wi-Fi bound the host kept its link, its clocks and its votes in every
+ * system suspend.  Upstream wants such root ports in D3 on non-x86
+ * (a5fb3ff63287, d4c79b63d82d in v7.3), through native pciehp.  This gives
+ * a qcom host's hot-plug root port without native pciehp bridge_d3, the D3
+ * that v7.3's PCI core gives it with native pciehp, as the PCI core
+ * enumerates it (and enumerates it again after a rescan):
+ * from the first suspend on the port goes to D3hot after its functions, the
+ * host sends PME_Turn_Off and powers down, and its resume sets it up again,
+ * trains the link and restores the functions' configuration
+ * (pci_pm_resume_noirq()).  It is the effect of the debug switch of
+ * pcie-qcom-debug-root-port-d3.patch (kit revision 11) from the boot, the
+ * boot's panel cycle (pm_test=platform) included.  bridge_d3 is recomputed
+ * only for a port the PCI core can put in D3 itself (pci_bridge_d3_update()),
+ * so it stays; the portdrv enables runtime PM only for a port
+ * pci_bridge_d3_possible() allows, so this adds no runtime D3.
+ * Nor is a function's D3cold veto consulted for the port then, nor
+ * pcie_port_pm=off: pcie_qcom.root_port_d3=0 on the command line leaves the
+ * ports as the PCI core has them; the debug switch's N takes it away at run
+ * time.  Without CONFIG_ACPI pciehp_is_native() is true and this does
+ * nothing (this port's configuration has CONFIG_ACPI).
+ */
+static bool qcom_pcie_root_port_d3 = true;
+module_param_named(root_port_d3, qcom_pcie_root_port_d3, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(root_port_d3,
+		 "Let the hot-plug root ports of qcom PCIe hosts without native pciehp go to D3hot in system suspend (default: Y)");
+
+static struct platform_driver qcom_pcie_driver;
+
+static void qcom_pcie_fixup_root_port_d3(struct pci_dev *pdev)
+{
+	struct pci_host_bridge *bridge;
+
+	if (!qcom_pcie_root_port_d3 || !pci_is_pcie(pdev) ||
+	    pci_pcie_type(pdev) != PCI_EXP_TYPE_ROOT_PORT)
+		return;
+
+	bridge = pci_find_host_bridge(pdev->bus);
+	if (!bridge || !bridge->dev.parent ||
+	    bridge->dev.parent->driver != &qcom_pcie_driver.driver)
+		return;
+
+	/* A hot-plug port without native pciehp: else the PCI core decides. */
+	if (pdev->bridge_d3 || !pdev->is_pciehp || pciehp_is_native(pdev))
+		return;
+
+	pdev->bridge_d3 = true;
+	pci_info(pdev, "goes to D3hot in system suspend (a hot-plug port without native pciehp; pcie_qcom.root_port_d3)\n");
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_CLASS_FINAL(PCI_ANY_ID, PCI_ANY_ID, PCI_CLASS_BRIDGE_PCI, 8,
+			      qcom_pcie_fixup_root_port_d3);
+
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qcom_pcie_pm_ops = {
 	NOIRQ_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq, qcom_pcie_resume_noirq)
 };
